  "statement": "The roots of $x^2-4x+1=0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find $\\alpha^3+\\beta^3$.",
  "solution": "By Vieta, $\\alpha+\\beta=4$ and $\\alpha\\beta=1$. Then $\\alpha^3+\\beta^3=(\\alpha+\\beta)^3-3\\alpha\\beta(\\alpha+\\beta)=64-3\\cdot1\\cdot4=52$.",
  "hints": [
    "Use Vieta's formulae for sum and product.",
    "Recall $\u0007lpha^3+\beta^3=S^3-3PS$."
  ],
